  "term": "escape mechanism",
  "definition": "In this biological context, an escape mechanism is a way tumor cells avoid detection or destruction by the immune system. Here, it refers to tumor cells shedding parts of MICA and MICB from their surface so NKG2D-expressing immune cells are less able to recognize them.",
